# Format and lint the staged files, then hold the gates that guard the
# conventions ESLint cannot express, then typecheck the project.
#
# The token and convention gates run against the whole tree rather than the
# staged subset: both are ratchets (scripts/*.baseline.json), and a partial
# view would let a violation move between files unnoticed.
#
# lint:plans is here rather than only in CI because the point of it is to
# make you update the plan in the SAME commit as the work. Catching it on
# push is too late — by then the commit that should have carried the update
# already exists.
npx lint-staged
npm run lint:tokens
npm run lint:conventions
npm run lint:plans
npm run typecheck
